{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfbw4wmvuhBKEc1ZysXMh", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Flags in this project are static booleans in a TOML file, read through one helper. I checked the convention against the code and it holds.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Declare:** add the flag to `flags.toml` under `[flags]`. The only existing one is `invoice-pdf-v2 = false`. Names are kebab-case.\n- **Read:** call `flags.is_on(\"name\")` from `src/flags.py`. Don't read the TOML directly.\n- **Loading:** `flags.toml` is read once, when `src/flags.py` is imported. Changing a flag means editing the file and restarting. There's no runtime toggle, percentage rollout or per-user targeting.\n- **Undeclared flags:** `is_on` returns `False` for a name that isn't in the file. A typo in a flag name silently reads as off, so check the name in both places.\n\n**For your checkout flow**\n1. Add `new-checkout-flow = false` to `flags.toml`.\n2. Branch where the checkout is chosen:\n   ```python\n   from src import flags\n\n   if flags.is_on(\"new-checkout-flow\"):\n       return new_checkout(...)\n   return legacy_checkout(...)\n   ```\n   Match the import style of the surrounding code. I didn't find any existing `is_on` callers to copy.\n3. Flip it to `true` to enable the flow.\n\nIf you need gradual rollout or per-user targeting, `flags.py` doesn't support it today. We'd have to extend it, and I can sketch that if you want."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 635, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25290, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 635}, "output_tokens": 489, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "98f7441e-64